    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d579">

                <pb facs="1060" n="1038" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg1038"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">357.AC/10–2650:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Syria</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Damascus</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-10-26T12:00:00+02:00">October 26,
                            1950—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>200. Re Deptel 143, October 17.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d579-f1"/> Legation believes Prime Minister Qudsi’s understanding
                    basis Syria coup [apparent omission] PRA is that
                    projects not be directly identified with resettlement refugees until political
                    settlement Palestine problem. While some Syrians may privately concede that
                    resettlement is not only inevitable but even desirable and while UNRWA projects must eventually be identified
                    with resettlement, it is doubtful if Syrians generally are psychologically
                    prepared to now move along as fast as reference telegram contemplates. There may
                    therefore be adverse reaction from government and press to blunt proposal that
                        UN funds be available only for “projects
                    initiated by NE governments which repatriate or
                    reestablish refugees”.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d579-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department 200, repeated info unnumbered, Beirut from Damascus.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jones</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d579-f1" n="1" xml:id="d579-f1-content">
                <p>This was a repeat of telegram 342 to Cairo, not printed; but see penultimate
                    paragraph of the editorial note on <ref target="#pg1023">p. 1023</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d579-f2" n="2" xml:id="d579-f2-content">
                <p>Taken from the sentence in telegram 141, which read as follows: “30 million as
                    initial contribution to a reintegration fund to be available only for projects
                    initiated by NE govts which repatriate or reestab
                    refugees.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
